12397.7s 191 The paper used its own data; our numbers are on the 498R All-in-One test split (different data),
12397.7s 192 so the comparison shows the direction and size of the gap, not a head-to-head result.
12397.7s 193 
12397.7s 194 The paper's 17 classes and 303 test crops (48 are copies of training crops, see the original check) vs our 101 tokens on the grouped split: a harder task, so a lower symbol accuracy is expected. The paper's plate score is the mean difflib SequenceMatcher ratio, which gives partial credit; plate exact is the strict number.
